<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8" ?><transcript><text start="12.1" dur="4.9">Ladies and gentlemen, the president of</text><text start="14.2" dur="5.8">the United States, Donald J. Trump,</text><text start="17" dur="6.7">accompanied by the president and CEO of</text><text start="20" dur="3.7">UFC, Dana White.</text><text start="65.6" dur="4">&amp;gt;&amp;gt; Well, thank you very much and</text><text start="67.5" dur="4.3">please be seated and enjoy yourselves.</text><text start="69.6" dur="4.7">This is to me great enjoyment because</text><text start="71.8" dur="3.9">we&amp;#39;re celebrating greatness</text><text start="74.3" dur="3.6">and these people and the people that</text><text start="75.7" dur="3.9">work with them.</text><text start="77.9" dur="4.6">Today is my</text><text start="79.6" dur="5.8">honor to welcome you all to our first</text><text start="82.5" dur="6.2">official event on the new</text><text start="85.4" dur="4.8">White House helipad. This is a big one.</text><text start="88.7" dur="2.9">I said, give me a helipad. I didn&amp;#39;t know</text><text start="90.2" dur="2.9">it was going to be this big, but people</text><text start="91.6" dur="4.5">love it. In fact, it&amp;#39;s so good I didn&amp;#39;t</text><text start="93.1" dur="4.5">even get sued when I built it.</text><text start="96.1" dur="3">That&amp;#39;s they wanted to sue. They had it</text><text start="97.6" dur="3.8">already. Then they saw it and they said,</text><text start="99.1" dur="3.7">bad, this thing is amazing.</text><text start="101.4" dur="2.9">And it&amp;#39;s all going to be amazing and</text><text start="102.8" dur="3.2">that&amp;#39;s going to be the most amazing of</text><text start="104.3" dur="3.7">all what we&amp;#39;re building for the White</text><text start="106" dur="4.7">House. They&amp;#39;ve been looking for that for</text><text start="108" dur="5.9">150 years, the ballroom</text><text start="110.7" dur="4.5">and the great military complex inside.</text><text start="113.9" dur="3.2">But this afternoon, I&amp;#39;m pleased to</text><text start="115.2" dur="5.292">announce that my good friend Dana White,</text><text start="117.1" dur="5.292">a legend, true a legend, what a man he</text><text start="120.492" dur="4.3">And I am personally presenting the</text><text start="122.392" dur="3.6">president&amp;#39;s own United States Marine</text><text start="124.792" dur="3.8">band</text><text start="125.992" dur="4.5">with a donation. Now it started off at</text><text start="128.592" dur="3.4">200,000</text><text start="130.492" dur="3.4">and I said how many people are there? I</text><text start="131.992" dur="3.9">thought there were 70</text><text start="133.892" dur="3.8">but it&amp;#39;s about 170. I don&amp;#39;t know a lot</text><text start="135.892" dur="3.9">of people joined.</text><text start="137.692" dur="3.3">So we decided to increase it, right</text><text start="139.792" dur="3.1">Dana?</text><text start="140.992" dur="4.4">So we were going to give 200,000 we&amp;#39;re</text><text start="142.892" dur="4.5">now making it 500,000. Now everyone&amp;#39;s</text><text start="145.392" dur="3.8">going to get a lot of money.</text><text start="147.392" dur="3.7">All right? That would</text><text start="149.192" dur="3.3">It took me about 1 second to get that</text><text start="151.092" dur="2.9">from Dana. I said do you want to go and</text><text start="152.492" dur="4.5">double up?</text><text start="153.992" dur="5.7">And it&amp;#39;s our honor because it&amp;#39;s</text><text start="156.992" dur="5.3">that&amp;#39;s a good little amount of money and</text><text start="159.692" dur="4.5">it&amp;#39;s on really fantastic. And this</text><text start="162.292" dur="4.2">really began because</text><text start="164.192" dur="5.5">Dana and I at the fight it&amp;#39;s the highest</text><text start="166.492" dur="4.6">rated fight in the history of this whole</text><text start="169.692" dur="2.5">world</text><text start="171.092" dur="3.1">but</text><text start="172.192" dur="3.4">the music was so good.</text><text start="174.192" dur="3">Now the fights were great and they were</text><text start="175.592" dur="3.3">among the best fights anyone&amp;#39;s ever</text><text start="177.192" dur="3.8">seen. That last fight</text><text start="178.892" dur="5.4">was the last two fights but you could</text><text start="180.992" dur="5.2">really see every single fight was ended</text><text start="184.292" dur="3.6">in knockouts all</text><text start="186.192" dur="2.9">and great champions. Everyone was a</text><text start="187.892" dur="2.7">champion</text><text start="189.092" dur="3.6">and it was the best night and it was</text><text start="190.592" dur="3.5">supposed to be a horrible horrible</text><text start="192.692" dur="2.4">weather. We didn&amp;#39;t know what was going</text><text start="194.092" dur="2.9">to happen.</text><text start="195.092" dur="3.9">In fact we delayed it because we thought</text><text start="196.992" dur="3.7">and if you lived a mile that way or a</text><text start="198.992" dur="3.2">mile that way</text><text start="200.692" dur="3.4">friends called me up they said how can</text><text start="202.192" dur="4.3">you be having a fight?</text><text start="204.092" dur="4.7">The clouds came and as soon as it got to</text><text start="206.492" dur="3.7">the White House right over there</text><text start="208.792" dur="2.9">they opened up</text><text start="210.192" dur="3.2">and everything was drenched. We didn&amp;#39;t</text><text start="211.692" dur="3.5">have one drop.</text><text start="213.392" dur="3.6">We were waiting. This was not good. We</text><text start="215.192" dur="4.7">said we&amp;#39;re in big trouble</text><text start="216.992" dur="4.5">but it was sort of a miracle evening and</text><text start="219.892" dur="3.9">with the White House in the background</text><text start="221.492" dur="3.4">and the ring was exactly here where this</text><text start="223.792" dur="2.7">was and</text><text start="224.892" dur="3.3">I started construction of this the</text><text start="226.492" dur="4.725">following day</text><text start="228.192" dur="4.5">and it&amp;#39;s exactly the size of the entire</text><text start="231.217" dur="4.175">[snorts] the entire ring and that was</text><text start="232.692" dur="4.2">some some fight. We had 100,000 people</text><text start="235.392" dur="4.4">in the park</text><text start="236.892" dur="4.5">and we had probably 6,000 7,000 people</text><text start="239.792" dur="2.6">here in front in the backdrop of the</text><text start="241.392" dur="2.402">White House.</text><text start="242.392" dur="3.202">I don&amp;#39;t think it&amp;#39;ll ever happen again,</text><text start="243.794" dur="4.1">Dana. I don&amp;#39;t think. And on top of it,</text><text start="245.594" dur="3.9">they were the best fights. Justin</text><text start="247.894" dur="4.3">Gaethje won.</text><text start="249.494" dur="4.3">And he was not favored.</text><text start="252.194" dur="3.3">And he fought the fight of his life and</text><text start="253.794" dur="4">he won.</text><text start="255.494" dur="3.6">Did a lot of damage. He won give a lot</text><text start="257.794" dur="2.6">of damage.</text><text start="259.094" dur="3">But people said it was among the</text><text start="260.394" dur="3.6">greatest events they&amp;#39;ve ever seen and it</text><text start="262.094" dur="4.2">was an honor to be there.</text><text start="263.994" dur="4.3">But the thing that was</text><text start="266.294" dur="4.2">equal to was the music, the quality of</text><text start="268.294" dur="3.3">the music. And Dana and I were walking</text><text start="270.494" dur="2.8">out</text><text start="271.594" dur="2.9">and</text><text start="273.294" dur="3.8">we heard</text><text start="274.494" dur="5.5">the cucaracha and we heard that was for</text><text start="277.094" dur="4.9">the Mexican champion who also won.</text><text start="279.994" dur="3.8">And we heard all these different songs,</text><text start="281.994" dur="3.8">most of which we knew, but it was better</text><text start="283.794" dur="3.7">than the original.</text><text start="285.794" dur="3.9">We thought it was a</text><text start="287.494" dur="4.6">recording. We said nobody could play</text><text start="289.694" dur="4.2">that well. And it turned out it was</text><text start="292.094" dur="3.2">these incredibly talented people that</text><text start="293.894" dur="2.9">are with us.</text><text start="295.294" dur="4.2">And I said, Dana, we got to give them a</text><text start="296.794" dur="4.9">big bonus here for the job they did.</text><text start="299.494" dur="4.4">And I mean, I will tell you, this wasn&amp;#39;t</text><text start="301.694" dur="4.5">doesn&amp;#39;t involve Dana as much, but they</text><text start="303.894" dur="4.2">also played for the</text><text start="306.194" dur="5.2">President of China who came here a few</text><text start="308.094" dur="4.8">weeks ago and for King Charles.</text><text start="311.394" dur="3.4">And they were unbelievable. They&amp;#39;re just</text><text start="312.894" dur="2.9">amazingly talented. Many of them could</text><text start="314.794" dur="2.9">be in</text><text start="315.794" dur="3.6">any of the greatest orchestras in the</text><text start="317.694" dur="2.9">world, Carnegie Hall. They could be</text><text start="319.394" dur="2.4">anywhere.</text><text start="320.594" dur="2.6">Many of them.</text><text start="321.794" dur="2.8">But they love the military. They love</text><text start="323.194" dur="4.3">our country.</text><text start="324.594" dur="5.5">So Dana and I are contributing</text><text start="327.494" dur="4.9">the $500,000</text><text start="330.094" dur="5.5">to express our immense appreciation for</text><text start="332.394" dur="5.3">your spectacular talent, unwavering</text><text start="335.594" dur="4.2">professionalism which it is, and total</text><text start="337.694" dur="4.2">commitment to excellence</text><text start="339.794" dur="3.7">in everything that you&amp;#39;ve done. And that</text><text start="341.894" dur="4.5">includes those people that make it</text><text start="343.494" dur="4.5">possible for you to play so well.</text><text start="346.394" dur="4.2">So as president,</text><text start="347.994" dur="4.5">I&amp;#39;ve admired you from the very first day</text><text start="350.594" dur="3.5">of my first term.</text><text start="352.494" dur="3.3">We&amp;#39;d have little events and you&amp;#39;d play</text><text start="354.094" dur="3.5">and I say, wow, they&amp;#39;re great. You I</text><text start="355.794" dur="3.3">mean, the bad part is you usually blew</text><text start="357.594" dur="4">away the artist. You know, we bring in</text><text start="359.094" dur="4.2">these big artists, Dana. Big names, but</text><text start="361.594" dur="3">they blow them away.</text><text start="363.294" dur="3.2">They they don&amp;#39;t even like going out</text><text start="364.594" dur="4.175">after watching you. You have more talent</text><text start="366.494" dur="4.295">than they do. I hate to tell you.</text><text start="368.769" dur="2.02">&amp;gt;&amp;gt; [snorts]</text><text start="408.069" dur="2.02">[snorts]</text><text start="443.895" dur="5.3">&amp;gt;&amp;gt; Really great job.</text><text start="446.295" dur="2.9">I&amp;#39;m so proud of you.</text><text start="449.495" dur="5.9">And we&amp;#39;re also pleased to be joined by</text><text start="451.595" dur="5.9">three people who I know you are very</text><text start="455.395" dur="3.7">familiar with and share my great</text><text start="457.495" dur="3.5">appreciation for this group&amp;#39;s</text><text start="459.095" dur="4.8">outstanding skill.</text><text start="460.995" dur="4">A man who is absolutely admired by most,</text><text start="463.895" dur="3.5">but</text><text start="464.995" dur="4.4">he does so well that they&amp;#39;re jealous.</text><text start="467.395" dur="3.8">And they want to get him, but they don&amp;#39;t</text><text start="469.395" dur="4.2">take him. They like you. They don&amp;#39;t take</text><text start="471.195" dur="4.4">him down very easily. He&amp;#39;s been actually</text><text start="473.595" dur="3.7">outstanding. So we won in Venezuela in</text><text start="475.595" dur="3.8">48 minutes.</text><text start="477.295" dur="4.1">And we&amp;#39;re knocking the hell out of him</text><text start="479.395" dur="3.9">in a And we&amp;#39;re being nice. We&amp;#39;re being</text><text start="481.395" dur="5.4">very nice, but they&amp;#39;re</text><text start="483.295" dur="5.802">Navy&amp;#39;s gone. Their Air Force is gone.</text><text start="486.795" dur="3.802">Frankly, their leaders are gone.</text><text start="489.097" dur="3.9">Everything&amp;#39;s gone.</text><text start="490.597" dur="3.9">And we&amp;#39;ll see how that</text><text start="492.997" dur="4.1">We&amp;#39;re being very nice. We&amp;#39;re being</text><text start="494.497" dur="4.1">patient. We&amp;#39;re being very patient.</text><text start="497.097" dur="3.9">But it&amp;#39;s been</text><text start="498.597" dur="4.4">amazing to watch him and</text><text start="500.997" dur="3.7">General Kane and all of the others. But</text><text start="502.997" dur="2.7">I want to just introduce Secretary of</text><text start="504.697" dur="3.4">War</text><text start="505.697" dur="6.2">Pete Hegseth, who has been a star. Thank</text><text start="508.097" dur="3.8">you, Pete. Thank you very much.</text><text start="512.997" dur="2.8">And he goes and he works out with the</text><text start="514.297" dur="2.8">guys, but I don&amp;#39;t know. He&amp;#39;s really in</text><text start="515.797" dur="3.3">good shape, but some of those guys are</text><text start="517.097" dur="2.978">tough, right? They&amp;#39;re tough to work out</text><text start="519.097" dur="4.3">with.</text><text start="520.075" dur="7.822">[snorts] Acting Secretary of the Navy</text><text start="523.397" dur="4.5">Hung Cao. Thank you. Thank you, Hung.</text><text start="528.897" dur="5.4">And the Commandant of the Marine Corps,</text><text start="530.997" dur="5.3">General Eric Smith. Thank you very much.</text><text start="534.297" dur="3.8">Thank you. Thank you, General. Central</text><text start="536.297" dur="3.6">Castle.</text><text start="538.097" dur="3.4">Looks like</text><text start="539.897" dur="3.8">He looks great.</text><text start="541.497" dur="4.2">And thanks as well to the Commanding</text><text start="543.697" dur="3.8">Officer of the Marine Barracks here in</text><text start="545.697" dur="4.4">Washington, Jason Copeland, and the</text><text start="547.497" dur="4.4">Marine Barracks Sergeant Major Juan</text><text start="550.097" dur="3.1">Segura. Thank you very much, fellas.</text><text start="551.897" dur="4.1">Thank you.</text><text start="553.197" dur="4.9">Thank you very much.</text><text start="555.997" dur="4.5">So each member of this elite military</text><text start="558.097" dur="4.9">band continued a</text><text start="560.497" dur="4.2">cherished part of the American musical</text><text start="562.997" dur="3.5">tradition, which is such a big deal</text><text start="564.697" dur="4.2">dating back</text><text start="566.497" dur="3.6">more than two centuries.</text><text start="568.897" dur="5.7">Incredible.</text><text start="570.097" dur="7">Founded in 1798. Now this is 1792, the</text><text start="574.597" dur="4.5">White House. So not so far back.</text><text start="577.097" dur="5.4">Think of that. 17 This was built in</text><text start="579.097" dur="5.2">1792, so you&amp;#39;re 1798.</text><text start="582.497" dur="4.3">By an act of Congress, the US Marine</text><text start="584.297" dur="3.9">Band has served every president except</text><text start="586.797" dur="3.2">George Washington. I don&amp;#39;t know what</text><text start="588.197" dur="3.8">happened there. A little bit You were a</text><text start="589.997" dur="4.9">little bit late for that one.</text><text start="591.997" dur="4.6">At state dinners and inaugurations</text><text start="594.897" dur="4.2">through great halls and</text><text start="596.597" dur="4.1">grand parades, the greatest parades</text><text start="599.097" dur="3.8">anyone&amp;#39;s ever seen.</text><text start="600.697" dur="4.1">You provided the soundtrack for American</text><text start="602.897" dur="3.7">history itself, and Dana has something</text><text start="604.797" dur="4.3">to tell you about that</text><text start="606.597" dur="4.701">because your performance during the UFC</text><text start="609.097" dur="4.501">fight has gotten tremendous</text><text start="611.298" dur="4">You&amp;#39;ll be talking about that, Dana.</text><text start="613.598" dur="3.7">The band was given its nickname, The</text><text start="615.298" dur="4.1">President&amp;#39;s Own,</text><text start="617.298" dur="4.2">by none other than Thomas Jefferson. I</text><text start="619.398" dur="4.1">wanted to say that cuz otherwise, when I</text><text start="621.498" dur="4.4">say The President&amp;#39;s Own, you&amp;#39;d say Trump</text><text start="623.498" dur="4.4">has an ego. This guy&amp;#39;s terrible. He&amp;#39;s</text><text start="625.898" dur="3.5">claiming the band now.</text><text start="627.898" dur="3.2">So this was long before me, The</text><text start="629.398" dur="3.3">President&amp;#39;s Own, but it&amp;#39;s called The</text><text start="631.098" dur="3.4">President&amp;#39;s Own.</text><text start="632.698" dur="3.8">It traveled with President Abraham</text><text start="634.498" dur="3">Lincoln to Gettysburg and</text><text start="636.498" dur="3.3">played</text><text start="637.498" dur="4.4">under the direction of the legendary</text><text start="639.798" dur="4.1">composer John</text><text start="641.898" dur="4.4">Philip Sousa. That&amp;#39;s a big deal and</text><text start="643.898" dur="5.4">you&amp;#39;re a national treasure. You really</text><text start="646.298" dur="4.8">are. You&amp;#39;re amazing, talented people.</text><text start="649.298" dur="3.8">Talent, you know? I have a friend Gary</text><text start="651.098" dur="3.7">Player is a great golfer. He says</text><text start="653.098" dur="3.1">talent, it&amp;#39;s all about talent. Well, you</text><text start="654.798" dur="3.6">have talent.</text><text start="656.198" dur="3">And today, The President&amp;#39;s Own is better</text><text start="658.398" dur="2.7">and</text><text start="659.198" dur="4">more talented, I believe, than ever</text><text start="661.098" dur="3.7">before. We very</text><text start="663.198" dur="3.2">very much</text><text start="664.798" dur="3.6">love and respect you. And by the way,</text><text start="666.398" dur="3.9">for everybody here, there are many, many</text><text start="668.398" dur="4.2">people that could turn down</text><text start="670.298" dur="4.9">either just can&amp;#39;t do it for some reason.</text><text start="672.598" dur="5.1">Mostly it is because of the talent. We</text><text start="675.198" dur="4.3">want the most talented people.</text><text start="677.698" dur="4">But in very exciting news, I want to</text><text start="679.498" dur="4.2">congratulate you on an unprecedented</text><text start="681.698" dur="3.6">accomplishment this week.</text><text start="683.698" dur="4.2">For the first time ever, the US Marine</text><text start="685.298" dur="5.2">Band has officially been nominated</text><text start="687.898" dur="4">for a Grammy Award and you&amp;#39;re going to</text><text start="690.498" dur="3.2">talk about that and you&amp;#39;re going to get</text><text start="691.898" dur="4.6">people to call in and vote cuz they</text><text start="693.698" dur="4.1">should win cuz I know a lot about music</text><text start="696.498" dur="2.8">and they&amp;#39;re better than the people that</text><text start="697.798" dur="3.4">are up.</text><text start="699.298" dur="4.6">But you&amp;#39;re in the nomination for best</text><text start="701.198" dur="4.5">orchestra performance for your recent</text><text start="703.898" dur="3.8">album</text><text start="705.698" dur="4.5">titled John Williams and The President&amp;#39;s</text><text start="707.698" dur="4.8">Own Volume Three. That&amp;#39;s a big That&amp;#39;s a</text><text start="710.198" dur="4.5">big deal. One of the many reasons I</text><text start="712.498" dur="5.5">wanted to give you this</text><text start="714.698" dur="4.8">special gift today is because I know how</text><text start="717.998" dur="3.6">hard you&amp;#39;ve been working and how hard</text><text start="719.498" dur="3.8">you work. I see it. I see it probably</text><text start="721.598" dur="4.1">more than anybody.</text><text start="723.298" dur="4.2">Over the past two years, you were a</text><text start="725.698" dur="3.4">memorable highlight</text><text start="727.498" dur="3.4">of my inauguration. You played</text><text start="729.098" dur="3.4">unbelievably. In fact, I wanted the</text><text start="730.898" dur="3.701">inauguration to go on for another hour.</text><text start="732.498" dur="3.501">I wanted to listen to your music, but</text><text start="734.599" dur="3.8">didn&amp;#39;t work out.</text><text start="735.999" dur="4.8">And you&amp;#39;ve performed God Save the King</text><text start="738.399" dur="6.1">for King Charles the Third. You sang</text><text start="740.799" dur="5.8">music from Les Mis for President</text><text start="744.499" dur="3.9">Xi of China. He still talked about it.</text><text start="746.599" dur="3.4">He talked about it yesterday when I was</text><text start="748.399" dur="3.9">with him. He said that band was</text><text start="749.999" dur="4.9">phenomenal cuz they also they had very</text><text start="752.299" dur="4.3">brilliant musicians. They gave us a</text><text start="754.899" dur="3.8">concert. They gave us a show that was</text><text start="756.599" dur="3.9">incredible also.</text><text start="758.699" dur="5">You headlined the celebration of</text><text start="760.499" dur="6">America&amp;#39;s 250th anniversary.</text><text start="763.699" dur="5.8">And you even mastered some new material</text><text start="766.499" dur="4.2">such as the one and only YMCA. You do it</text><text start="769.499" dur="2.8">very well.</text><text start="770.699" dur="2.8">That&amp;#39;s become quite successful. You</text><text start="772.299" dur="3.2">know, that was</text><text start="773.499" dur="3.5">32 years ago. That was number five.</text><text start="775.499" dur="3.5">Didn&amp;#39;t hit number one.</text><text start="776.999" dur="4.1">But for many months it was number one.</text><text start="778.999" dur="4.2">So it was 32. The difference was they</text><text start="781.099" dur="3.9">got a little bit heavier</text><text start="783.199" dur="3.7">as a band. The band it looked a little</text><text start="784.999" dur="3.4">bit different, not totally recognizable,</text><text start="786.899" dur="3.9">but they&amp;#39;re great guys and they loved</text><text start="788.399" dur="3.7">it. They weigh a couple of pounds more</text><text start="790.799" dur="4.1">than they did.</text><text start="792.099" dur="4.4">But uh it went from number five, which</text><text start="794.899" dur="3.2">was a big hit, but it was number five.</text><text start="796.499" dur="3.2">Didn&amp;#39;t hit number one.</text><text start="798.099" dur="3.8">But it hit number one for a long time</text><text start="799.699" dur="3.8">with us. So when you think of it, it&amp;#39;s</text><text start="801.899" dur="3.6">pretty amazing, right? That a song you&amp;#39;d</text><text start="803.499" dur="3.9">bring it back and it became</text><text start="805.499" dur="3.8">a smash, which tells you the power of</text><text start="807.399" dur="3.6">politics, doesn&amp;#39;t it?</text><text start="809.299" dur="3.8">And next month we&amp;#39;re looking forward to</text><text start="810.999" dur="4.7">having the President&amp;#39;s own perform for</text><text start="813.099" dur="6">dozens of top world leaders when they</text><text start="815.699" dur="4.8">host the G20 conference in Florida in</text><text start="819.099" dur="2.9">Doral.</text><text start="820.499" dur="4.2">And it&amp;#39;s going to be great. We have all</text><text start="821.999" dur="4.2">the the top 20 leaders in the world</text><text start="824.699" dur="5.2">going to be there.</text><text start="826.199" dur="6.3">So it&amp;#39;s a true honor to have you perform</text><text start="829.899" dur="4.2">for us. You know, when I when I said the</text><text start="832.499" dur="2.8">money we didn&amp;#39;t think about this. I only</text><text start="834.099" dur="2">said it this morning. I said, what are</text><text start="835.299" dur="2.8">we going to do? Well, you&amp;#39;re just going</text><text start="836.099" dur="3.1">to have a minor ceremony.</text><text start="838.099" dur="3">And I want to thank Chamberlain,</text><text start="839.199" dur="3.9">wherever she may be, cuz she put this</text><text start="841.099" dur="3.4">all together very quickly.</text><text start="843.099" dur="3.3">And I said, well, are they going to</text><text start="844.499" dur="3.1">play? No, they weren&amp;#39;t. I said, wait a</text><text start="846.399" dur="3.3">minute, I&amp;#39;m giving them a lot of money.</text><text start="847.599" dur="4">We&amp;#39;re going to up it to 500,000. Let</text><text start="849.699" dur="3.8">them make like let them play a little</text><text start="851.599" dur="3.1">music. Do you agree?</text><text start="853.499" dur="2.802">So uh</text><text start="854.699" dur="3.902">this was all sort of put together. Then</text><text start="856.301" dur="4.5">I said, let&amp;#39;s invite the press. So we</text><text start="858.601" dur="4.8">actually invited the press. Often times</text><text start="860.801" dur="5.3">not my favorite people, but that&amp;#39;s okay.</text><text start="863.401" dur="6.1">And they were all excited and we have</text><text start="866.101" dur="6.3">really very some good stuff done by your</text><text start="869.501" dur="5.3">your commissary, by people that love you</text><text start="872.401" dur="4.4">and they love making good food for you.</text><text start="874.801" dur="4">So I want you to know that we&amp;#39;re very</text><text start="876.801" dur="5">grateful and that</text><text start="878.801" dur="5.2">John Philip Sousa famously said</text><text start="881.801" dur="5.4">and wanted his own orchestra to be as</text><text start="884.001" dur="4.7">great among bands as any there are in</text><text start="887.201" dur="3.1">America.</text><text start="888.701" dur="3.3">And he said it and you know what that&amp;#39;s</text><text start="890.301" dur="3.9">turned out to be true because friends of</text><text start="892.001" dur="4">mine that are in the music business said</text><text start="894.201" dur="3.7">that were here that night,</text><text start="896.001" dur="4.2">but at other times also they said they</text><text start="897.901" dur="5.1">are as good as it gets. So it&amp;#39;s a big</text><text start="900.201" dur="4.3">deal. So we put this together and I said</text><text start="903.001" dur="2.8">to Dana, we got to make them work a</text><text start="904.501" dur="3">little bit. So they&amp;#39;re going to play a</text><text start="905.801" dur="3.2">few songs for us.</text><text start="907.501" dur="3.7">And</text><text start="909.001" dur="3.9">it&amp;#39;s something that everybody here, we</text><text start="911.201" dur="3.2">have the cabinet here.</text><text start="912.901" dur="3.7">We have the leaders here. We have a lot</text><text start="914.401" dur="3.7">of generals here, a lot of great</text><text start="916.601" dur="4.1">We have two great admirals here that I</text><text start="918.101" dur="4.6">know and respect and we&amp;#39;re doing so</text><text start="920.701" dur="3.5">well. They&amp;#39;ve got that great talent for</text><text start="922.701" dur="3.3">something else. It&amp;#39;s called warfare,</text><text start="924.201" dur="3.7">which is what we want.</text><text start="926.001" dur="3.6">So now I&amp;#39;d like to ask my friend Dana</text><text start="927.901" dur="3.3">White, one of the true legends, the most</text><text start="929.601" dur="4">successful</text><text start="931.201" dur="4">promoter of fights, but really I think I</text><text start="933.601" dur="3.7">could say the most successful promoter</text><text start="935.201" dur="4.1">of anything, frankly.</text><text start="937.301" dur="4">What he&amp;#39;s been able to do is really</text><text start="939.301" dur="3.3">incredible and then I&amp;#39;m going to hand</text><text start="941.301" dur="4.2">out the</text><text start="942.601" dur="4.1">check along with Dana to director Ryan</text><text start="945.501" dur="3.3">Nolen.</text><text start="946.701" dur="4.1">And Dana, if you could</text><text start="948.801" dur="3.6">come forward and say a few words, I&amp;#39;d</text><text start="950.801" dur="4.5">love to listen. I could listen to this</text><text start="952.401" dur="4.9">guy all day because he&amp;#39;s an inspiration.</text><text start="955.301" dur="3.3">He&amp;#39;s an inspiration, respected by</text><text start="957.301" dur="3.3">everybody,</text><text start="958.601" dur="3.3">respected by the toughest people in the</text><text start="960.601" dur="3">world because I think they might be the</text><text start="961.901" dur="3.6">toughest. You don&amp;#39;t get any tougher than</text><text start="963.601" dur="4.1">them. But</text><text start="965.501" dur="4.8">everybody loves and respects Dana White.</text><text start="967.701" dur="2.6">Thank you, Dana.</text><text start="971.376" dur="2.02">&amp;gt;&amp;gt; [applause]</text><text start="975.801" dur="5.201">&amp;gt;&amp;gt; Thank you, Mr. President.</text><text start="978.202" dur="5.7">This band prepared for Freedom</text><text start="981.002" dur="5.6">250 like it was a military operation.</text><text start="983.902" dur="5.7">Eight weeks of planning, 39 songs from</text><text start="986.602" dur="4.7">32 different artists, many with custom</text><text start="989.602" dur="4.3">arrangements, and</text><text start="991.302" dur="4.8">in the days before the event, they spent</text><text start="993.902" dur="4.5">four full days rehearsing with our</text><text start="996.102" dur="4.5">production in the blazing sun and</text><text start="998.402" dur="4.2">humidity here in DC.</text><text start="1000.602" dur="3">My head of production Craig Borsari said</text><text start="1002.602" dur="2.8">that</text><text start="1003.602" dur="4.3">when they would take breaks, these guys</text><text start="1005.402" dur="4.6">were in full military dress rehearsing</text><text start="1007.902" dur="3.8">in the sun. When they would get up, the</text><text start="1010.002" dur="3.4">seats were soaked.</text><text start="1011.702" dur="3.2">No complaints, not one complaint the</text><text start="1013.402" dur="2.7">entire time.</text><text start="1014.902" dur="3">Now, I&amp;#39;ve worked with a lot of great</text><text start="1016.102" dur="4">teams, and I know what it looks like</text><text start="1017.902" dur="3.9">when people take pride in their work. I</text><text start="1020.102" dur="3.2">saw it in the way the Marines handled</text><text start="1021.802" dur="3.5">every rehearsal,</text><text start="1023.302" dur="4.8">and I heard it in every song that was</text><text start="1025.302" dur="4.4">played at Freedom 250.</text><text start="1028.102" dur="3.4">There were times, like the President</text><text start="1029.702" dur="4.3">said,</text><text start="1031.502" dur="4.6">a song would be playing, and I would go,</text><text start="1034.002" dur="3.6">is that the DJ? Is the DJ playing? And</text><text start="1036.102" dur="3.4">you look over,</text><text start="1037.602" dur="4.8">and it was the band. And it sounded</text><text start="1039.502" dur="4.6">exactly like the artist.</text><text start="1042.402" dur="2.9">Uh it was it was really amazing. And I</text><text start="1044.102" dur="3.4">want to thank</text><text start="1045.302" dur="5">uh [snorts] Lieutenant Colonel Ryan</text><text start="1047.502" dur="5.7">Nalen. I want to thank Lieutenant</text><text start="1050.302" dur="5.5">Colonel Douglas Beryan,</text><text start="1053.202" dur="4.8">Gunnery Sergeant Scott Nimner, and every</text><text start="1055.802" dur="5">musician and crew member who helped pull</text><text start="1058.002" dur="6.3">this off, including those who joined us</text><text start="1060.802" dur="5.2">from Army, Navy, and Air Force.</text><text start="1064.302" dur="2.7">Now, a couple things I want to point out</text><text start="1066.002" dur="2.5">that are</text><text start="1067.002" dur="4">truly incredible.</text><text start="1068.502" dur="5.3">The album is available. The UFC Freedom</text><text start="1071.002" dur="6.3">250 album is available worldwide, and it</text><text start="1073.802" dur="5.65">has 4 million streams right now.</text><text start="1077.302" dur="3.9">Now, we have a big music department</text><text start="1079.452" dur="4.85">[snorts] at TKR our company. We have the</text><text start="1081.202" dur="4.7">WWE and the UFC, and we use a lot of</text><text start="1084.302" dur="4.2">music.</text><text start="1085.902" dur="5.9">And my music guys are telling me the</text><text start="1088.502" dur="5.7">fact that UFC Freedom 250 music made it</text><text start="1091.802" dur="3.7">to the first round of voting in the</text><text start="1094.202" dur="4">Grammys</text><text start="1095.502" dur="4.701">for album of the year is absolutely</text><text start="1098.202" dur="3.801">unbelievable and incredible. So,</text><text start="1100.203" dur="4.2">congratulations</text><text start="1102.003" dur="3.4">to you Marines. And like the President</text><text start="1104.403" dur="2.7">said,</text><text start="1105.403" dur="3.9">I hope you guys win. It would be</text><text start="1107.103" dur="4.5">absolutely incredible.</text><text start="1109.303" dur="4">Um, so on behalf of everybody at the</text><text start="1111.603" dur="3.9">UFC,</text><text start="1113.303" dur="4.3">thank you for the hours you put in.</text><text start="1115.503" dur="5">Thank you for your service and thank you</text><text start="1117.603" dur="5.1">for giving UFC Freedom 250 a sound of</text><text start="1120.503" dur="4.4">its own. It&amp;#39;s been an absolute honor to</text><text start="1122.703" dur="5.5">work with you.</text><text start="1124.903" dur="3.3">Now I would like Thank you.</text><text start="1130.703" dur="5.1">Now I&amp;#39;d like to introduce Lieutenant</text><text start="1132.403" dur="3.4">Colonel Ryan Nalen.</text><text start="1137.748" dur="2.02">&amp;gt;&amp;gt; [applause]</text><text start="1144.953" dur="2.02">[applause]</text><text start="1149.003" dur="4">&amp;gt;&amp;gt; Good afternoon, ladies and gentlemen.</text><text start="1150.403" dur="4.8">Mr. President, Mr. White, thank you very</text><text start="1153.003" dur="4.7">much for your generosity and for your</text><text start="1155.203" dur="4.8">continued support of this incredible</text><text start="1157.703" dur="3.7">organization. Commandant, thank you for</text><text start="1160.003" dur="3">your support and being here. Speaker</text><text start="1161.403" dur="2.9">Johnson, you honor us with your</text><text start="1163.003" dur="3.7">presence.</text><text start="1164.303" dur="5.5">Mr. Secretary, appreciate your support</text><text start="1166.703" dur="5.2">as well. And uh Secretary uh Cao, thank</text><text start="1169.803" dur="5.3">you for being here. Friends, Marine</text><text start="1171.903" dur="6">Band, this party is for you.</text><text start="1175.103" dur="5.2">We are so grateful for the opportunity</text><text start="1177.903" dur="4.6">to perform for you today, Mr. President.</text><text start="1180.303" dur="5.3">We&amp;#39;re so grateful for your continued</text><text start="1182.503" dur="4.8">support of music, the arts, and the</text><text start="1185.603" dur="3.9">United States Marine Band. We have a</text><text start="1187.303" dur="3.6">special program that we&amp;#39;ve put together</text><text start="1189.503" dur="4.6">for you.</text><text start="1190.903" dur="4.9">This organization dates back to 1798,</text><text start="1194.103" dur="3.7">the beginnings of our country, as the</text><text start="1195.803" dur="3.5">President said. And the thing that I</text><text start="1197.803" dur="3.4">love most, if I had to pick something I</text><text start="1199.303" dur="4.2">love most about the United States Marine</text><text start="1201.203" dur="5">Band, is when I hear them play,</text><text start="1203.503" dur="4.6">it&amp;#39;s an unbroken lineage. The people</text><text start="1206.203" dur="4.1">that you hear playing have played with</text><text start="1208.103" dur="4.4">people who have played with people who</text><text start="1210.303" dur="4">have played for John Philip Sousa, who</text><text start="1212.503" dur="3.1">played to the founding of our country.</text><text start="1214.303" dur="3">And if you think about how you learn</text><text start="1215.603" dur="4.5">music</text><text start="1217.303" dur="5">and play in an ensemble, you sit and you</text><text start="1220.103" dur="4.902">have the music printed in front of you,</text><text start="1222.303" dur="5.002">but you feed off of your musicians, you</text><text start="1225.005" dur="5.2">feed the musicians, and it&amp;#39;s passed down</text><text start="1227.305" dur="5.7">generation to generation, hand to hand,</text><text start="1230.205" dur="5.3">heart to heart, and it is the living</text><text start="1233.005" dur="4.9">embodiment of American history and</text><text start="1235.505" dur="4.8">American musical history in these</text><text start="1237.905" dur="4.3">musicians. It&amp;#39;s an American treasure,</text><text start="1240.305" dur="4.2">and Mr. President, you recognized that,</text><text start="1242.205" dur="4.3">you recognized that today. Mr. White,</text><text start="1244.505" dur="3.8">you heard that at the UFC fight and all</text><text start="1246.505" dur="4">of these other events, and it is our</text><text start="1248.305" dur="3.8">honor to serve in this incredibly</text><text start="1250.505" dur="3.7">special way.</text><text start="1252.105" dur="3.6">This is America&amp;#39;s band.</text><text start="1254.205" dur="3">We want to bring it to every home, to</text><text start="1255.705" dur="4.1">every heart. The Marine Band can do</text><text start="1257.205" dur="4.5">something for everyone in our country,</text><text start="1259.805" dur="4">for every veteran, for every grieving</text><text start="1261.705" dur="3.9">family, for every music enthusiast, for</text><text start="1263.805" dur="4">every music student, for every music</text><text start="1265.605" dur="3.9">teacher. The Marine Band is there for</text><text start="1267.805" dur="3.7">you, just as we are for you, Mr.</text><text start="1269.505" dur="5.2">President. It is an honor to serve in</text><text start="1271.505" dur="6.2">this way, and we cannot thank you enough</text><text start="1274.705" dur="6.489">uh for this unbelievable reception here</text><text start="1277.705" dur="5.509">today. Thank you, Mr. President.</text><text start="1281.194" dur="2.02">&amp;gt;&amp;gt; [applause]</text><text start="1290.364" dur="2.02">[applause]</text><text start="1294.949" dur="2.02">[applause]</text><text start="1304.119" dur="2.02">[applause]</text><text start="1342.765" dur="2.02">[applause]</text><text start="1351.935" dur="2.02">[applause]</text><text start="1361.105" dur="2.02">[applause]</text><text start="1366.345" dur="2.02">[applause]</text><text start="1374.86" dur="2.02">[applause]</text><text start="1379.445" dur="2.02">[applause]</text><text start="1390.006" dur="4.3">&amp;gt;&amp;gt; So thank you very much. I was just</text><text start="1391.806" dur="4.4">noticing as I sat and I&amp;#39;m staring at</text><text start="1394.306" dur="3.7">that beautiful building.</text><text start="1396.206" dur="4.2">If you would have seen that building two</text><text start="1398.006" dur="4.5">years ago, it wasn&amp;#39;t looking so good.</text><text start="1400.406" dur="3.6">But through a lot of talent within all</text><text start="1402.506" dur="2.4">within the</text><text start="1404.006" dur="2">uh</text><text start="1404.906" dur="3.7">I guess you could say the great</text><text start="1406.006" dur="4.7">professionals here, the Department of</text><text start="1408.606" dur="4.7">Interior. Thank you very much Greg and</text><text start="1410.706" dur="4.7">everybody and Doug, Doug Burgum.</text><text start="1413.306" dur="3.6">Uh but we worked very hard on bringing</text><text start="1415.406" dur="3.1">the White House back</text><text start="1416.906" dur="3.3">and it&amp;#39;s now more beautiful in better</text><text start="1418.506" dur="4.7">shape. A lot of the moldings were</text><text start="1420.206" dur="4.9">missing. Windows were broken. We had 17</text><text start="1423.206" dur="3.4">windows that were broken.</text><text start="1425.106" dur="2.9">And we took a little heat because they</text><text start="1426.606" dur="2.8">said, oh he&amp;#39;s devoting time. I didn&amp;#39;t</text><text start="1428.006" dur="3.3">devote much time, but I know how to do</text><text start="1429.406" dur="3.5">this. But I&amp;#39;m sitting there looking at</text><text start="1431.306" dur="4.5">how gorgeous that building is. And</text><text start="1432.906" dur="4.7">remember, the White House is maybe the</text><text start="1435.806" dur="4">number one just about the number one</text><text start="1437.606" dur="3.7">symbol of our country. And now when you</text><text start="1439.806" dur="4.7">look at it, it&amp;#39;s pristine, more</text><text start="1441.306" dur="5.2">beautiful than it was in 1792 and better</text><text start="1444.506" dur="3.9">shape. So it&amp;#39;s an honor to have done</text><text start="1446.506" dur="3.6">that. And now what we&amp;#39;d like to do is</text><text start="1448.406" dur="4.4">hear some great music. Thank you very</text><text start="1450.106" dur="4.72">much everybody. Thank you.</text><text start="1452.806" dur="2.02">&amp;gt;&amp;gt; [applause]</text><text start="1486.867" dur="2.02">[music]</text><text start="1498.002" dur="2.02">[music]</text><text start="1509.792" dur="2.02">[music]</text><text start="1528.132" dur="2.02">[music]</text><text start="1541.887" dur="2.02">[music]</text><text start="1550.402" dur="2.02">[music]</text><text start="1557.607" dur="2.02">[music]</text><text start="1566.122" dur="2.021">[music]</text><text start="1577.258" dur="2.02">[music]</text><text start="1594.943" dur="2.02">[music]</text><text start="1606.078" dur="2.02">[music]</text><text start="1610.663" dur="2.02">[music]</text><text start="1626.383" dur="2.02">[music]</text><text start="1634.243" dur="2.02">[music]</text><text start="1647.998" dur="2.02">[music]</text><text start="1657.824" dur="2.02">[music]</text><text start="1666.994" dur="2.02">[applause]</text><text start="1673.409" dur="3.7">&amp;gt;&amp;gt; Thank you very much. That was John</text><text start="1674.909" dur="4.5">Philip Sousa&amp;#39;s most famous march and our</text><text start="1677.109" dur="4.6">national march, The Stars and Stripes</text><text start="1679.409" dur="4">Forever. We&amp;#39;ll move on now to a piece</text><text start="1681.709" dur="3.8">that was written for the Marine Band in</text><text start="1683.409" dur="6.4">honor of the United States Marine Corps.</text><text start="1685.509" dur="4.3">This is Robert Jager&amp;#39;s Esprit de Corps.</text><text start="1720.704" dur="2.02">&amp;gt;&amp;gt; [music]</text><text start="1727.254" dur="2.02">[music]</text><text start="1731.839" dur="2.02">[music]</text><text start="1739.044" dur="2.021">[music]</text><text start="1746.905" dur="2.02">[music]</text><text start="1752.8" dur="2.02">[music]</text><text start="1762.625" dur="2.02">[music]</text><text start="1771.14" dur="2.02">[music]</text><text start="1783.585" dur="2.02">[music]</text><text start="1790.135" dur="2.02">[music]</text><text start="1803.89" dur="2.02">[music]</text><text start="1845.156" dur="2.02">[music]</text><text start="1848.112" dur="2">&amp;gt;&amp;gt; Oh</text><text start="1856.946" dur="2.02">&amp;gt;&amp;gt; [music]</text><text start="1867.426" dur="2.02">[music]</text><text start="1873.976" dur="2.02">[music]</text><text start="1886.421" dur="2.02">[music]</text><text start="1892.316" dur="2.02">[music]</text><text start="1900.831" dur="2.02">[music]</text><text start="1908.036" dur="2.02">[music]</text><text start="1955.197" dur="2.02">[music]</text><text start="1959.782" dur="2.02">[music]</text><text start="1968.297" dur="2.02">[music]</text><text start="1975.502" dur="2.02">[music]</text><text start="1992.532" dur="2.02">[applause]</text><text start="1998.513" dur="3.8">&amp;gt;&amp;gt; We&amp;#39;re so proud to</text><text start="2000.013" dur="5.7">serve in our country in this way through</text><text start="2002.313" dur="6">our music as are so many so many around</text><text start="2005.713" dur="4.9">the world. Our next piece honors</text><text start="2008.313" dur="4.3">all service members, anyone who has</text><text start="2010.613" dur="5.7">served, all of those who have been</text><text start="2012.613" dur="5.8">impacted by service now or back in their</text><text start="2016.313" dur="4.6">families generations. This piece is</text><text start="2018.413" dur="4.9">called Let Freedom Ring and is a piece I</text><text start="2020.913" dur="4.1">composed based on the famous melody My</text><text start="2023.313" dur="3.4">Country, &amp;#39;Tis of Thee.</text><text start="2025.013" dur="4.1">I focused on the lyric Land Where My</text><text start="2026.713" dur="3.9">Fathers Died because not a day goes by</text><text start="2029.113" dur="4.4">that we don&amp;#39;t think of those who have</text><text start="2030.613" dur="4.8">sacrificed for us to be able to have the</text><text start="2033.513" dur="5.4">freedoms that we have today.</text><text start="2035.413" dur="3.5">This is Let Freedom Ring.</text><text start="2053.448" dur="2.02">&amp;gt;&amp;gt; [music]</text><text start="2063.273" dur="2.02">[music]</text><text start="2073.753" dur="2.02">[music]</text><text start="2079.648" dur="2.021">[music]</text><text start="2090.128" dur="2.02">[music]</text><text start="2098.644" dur="2.02">[music]</text><text start="2109.124" dur="2.02">[music]</text><text start="2143.184" dur="2.02">[music]</text><text start="2151.699" dur="2.02">[music]</text><text start="2156.939" dur="2.02">[music]</text><text start="2162.834" dur="2.02">[music]</text><text start="2168.075" dur="2.02">[music]</text><text start="2181.175" dur="2.02">[music]</text><text start="2190.345" dur="2.02">[music]</text><text start="2205.41" dur="2.02">[music]</text><text start="2230.3" dur="2.02">[music]</text><text start="2235.54" dur="2.02">[music]</text><text start="2244.71" dur="2.02">[music]</text><text start="2251.915" dur="2.02">[music]</text><text start="2264.361" dur="2.02">[music]</text><text start="2278.116" dur="2.02">[applause]</text><text start="2289.416" dur="3.2">&amp;gt;&amp;gt; Thank you ladies and gentlemen. Going to</text><text start="2291.216" dur="3.9">move to something a little different</text><text start="2292.616" dur="5.2">now. I&amp;#39;d like to welcome up one of our</text><text start="2295.116" dur="4.9">vocalists to the stage.</text><text start="2297.816" dur="5.8">This next piece is a setting of Amazing</text><text start="2300.016" dur="5.5">Grace. This Amazing Grace is for our</text><text start="2303.616" dur="3.3">everyone, but it is also in honor of our</text><text start="2305.516" dur="3.6">beloved Marine Corps. And if you listen</text><text start="2306.916" dur="4.7">closely, you&amp;#39;ll hear us slowly</text><text start="2309.116" dur="4">insert elements of the Marines hymn</text><text start="2311.616" dur="2.5">throughout the course of this Amazing</text><text start="2313.116" dur="3.4">Grace.</text><text start="2314.116" dur="4.7">And it&amp;#39;s my pleasure to welcome to sing</text><text start="2316.516" dur="4.8">this rendition arranged of Amazing</text><text start="2318.816" dur="4.7">Grace, our very own Mr. White, you know</text><text start="2321.316" dur="4.8">her very well, Staff Sergeant Hannah</text><text start="2323.516" dur="2.6">Davis.</text><text start="2327.241" dur="2.02">&amp;gt;&amp;gt; [applause]</text><text start="2352.787" dur="2.02">[music]</text><text start="2358.682" dur="2.02">[music]</text><text start="2365.232" dur="3.985">[music]</text><text start="2366.517" dur="2.7">&amp;gt;&amp;gt; Amazing [singing]</text><text start="2369.317" dur="4.43">grace,</text><text start="2371.127" dur="5.49">[music] how sweet</text><text start="2373.747" dur="5.47">[singing] the sound</text><text start="2376.617" dur="5">that saved</text><text start="2379.217" dur="6.2">a wretch</text><text start="2381.617" dur="3.8">like me.</text><text start="2387.117" dur="4.9">I once</text><text start="2389.417" dur="5.29">was lost,</text><text start="2392.017" dur="5.1">but now</text><text start="2394.707" dur="5.11">[singing] I&amp;#39;m found.</text><text start="2397.117" dur="5.4">Was blind,</text><text start="2399.817" dur="6.5">but [singing] now</text><text start="2402.517" dur="3.8">I see.</text><text start="2407.152" dur="3.33">[singing]</text><text start="2408.462" dur="2.02">[music]</text><text start="2422.872" dur="2.02">[music]</text><text start="2428.417" dur="5.1">&amp;#39;Twas grace [singing]</text><text start="2431.217" dur="4.6">that taught</text><text start="2433.517" dur="4.7">my heart</text><text start="2435.817" dur="4.8">to fear, [singing]</text><text start="2438.217" dur="7.581">and grace</text><text start="2440.617" dur="7.201">my fears relieved.</text><text start="2445.798" dur="2.02">[music]</text><text start="2447.917" dur="5.101">How precious [screaming]</text><text start="2451.038" dur="4.585">[singing] did</text><text start="2453.018" dur="4.9">that grace</text><text start="2455.623" dur="7.295">[singing] appear [music]</text><text start="2457.918" dur="7.585">the hour I first</text><text start="2462.918" dur="2.585">believed. [singing]</text><text start="2475.273" dur="2.02">[music]</text><text start="2484.443" dur="2.02">[music]</text><text start="2487.518" dur="5.4">Through many [singing]</text><text start="2490.993" dur="5.825">[screaming]</text><text start="2492.918" dur="6.8">dangers, toils and [singing] snares,</text><text start="2496.818" dur="2.9">I have</text><text start="2499.818" dur="4.6">already</text><text start="2502.318" dur="2.1">come.</text><text start="2509.118" dur="2.8">&amp;#39;Twas</text><text start="2509.988" dur="3.73">[screaming] grace</text><text start="2511.918" dur="6">that brought</text><text start="2513.718" dur="6.5">me [singing] safe thus far,</text><text start="2517.918" dur="5.2">and grace</text><text start="2520.218" dur="5">will lead me</text><text start="2523.118" dur="2.1">home.</text><text start="2532.318" dur="5.8">And grace</text><text start="2535.018" dur="6.1">will [singing] lead</text><text start="2538.118" dur="3">me</text><text start="2541.518" dur="2.586">home. [singing]</text><text start="2546.014" dur="2.02">[music]</text><text start="2550.599" dur="2.02">&amp;gt;&amp;gt; [music]</text><text start="2566.974" dur="2.02">[applause]</text><text start="2576.82" dur="4.2">&amp;gt;&amp;gt; Thank you. Thank you all very much.</text><text start="2579.22" dur="4.3">Staff Sergeant Hannah Davis, ladies and</text><text start="2581.02" dur="2.5">gentlemen.</text><text start="2589.72" dur="3.2">We&amp;#39;re going to keep Hannah here singing</text><text start="2591.22" dur="3.5">for you just for two our final two</text><text start="2592.92" dur="4.2">selections. First, Mr. President, your</text><text start="2594.72" dur="4.8">request for Miss Davis and for you, this</text><text start="2597.12" dur="6.1">is America the Beautiful. And we&amp;#39;ll</text><text start="2599.52" dur="5.9">follow that with uh God Bless America,</text><text start="2603.22" dur="4.8">which will invite you all to join us in</text><text start="2605.42" dur="4.5">singing along. Mr. President, Mr. White,</text><text start="2608.02" dur="4.2">everybody, thank you very much for this</text><text start="2609.92" dur="4.7">opportunity to be here today for</text><text start="2612.22" dur="5.7">receiving us so kindly and acknowledging</text><text start="2614.62" dur="5.6">these incredible musicians that I have</text><text start="2617.92" dur="4">just the blessed opportunity to lead.</text><text start="2620.22" dur="3.2">It&amp;#39;s a stewardship. Take care of the</text><text start="2621.92" dur="3.1">organization as long as it&amp;#39;s been</text><text start="2623.42" dur="3.9">entrusted to me and I&amp;#39;m very grateful</text><text start="2625.02" dur="4.3">for that opportunity. So thank you very</text><text start="2627.32" dur="4.6">very much. This is America the</text><text start="2629.32" dur="2.6">Beautiful.</text><text start="2656.055" dur="2.02">&amp;gt;&amp;gt; [music]</text><text start="2661.295" dur="2.02">[music]</text><text start="2666.62" dur="6.2">&amp;gt;&amp;gt; Oh beautiful [singing]</text><text start="2670.22" dur="3.7">for spacious</text><text start="2672.82" dur="8.3">skies, [music]</text><text start="2673.92" dur="9.645">for amber waves [singing] of grain,</text><text start="2681.12" dur="4.4">for purple</text><text start="2683.565" dur="3.93">[singing] mountain</text><text start="2685.52" dur="2.8">majesties</text><text start="2687.495" dur="2.925">[music]</text><text start="2688.32" dur="2.1">above</text><text start="2690.82" dur="3.941">the fruit</text><text start="2692.62" dur="2.141">and plain. [singing]</text><text start="2695.721" dur="2.5">America,</text><text start="2699.941" dur="9.48">[singing] America,</text><text start="2702.921" dur="6.5">God shed his grace on [singing] thee,</text><text start="2710.321" dur="7.6">and crown</text><text start="2712.821" dur="5.1">thy [singing] good with brotherhood</text><text start="2718.321" dur="5.855">from sea to</text><text start="2722.921" dur="3.275">sea.</text><text start="2724.176" dur="2.02">[singing]</text><text start="2731.381" dur="2.02">[music]</text><text start="2738.586" dur="2.02">[music]</text><text start="2747.421" dur="4.1">Oh,</text><text start="2748.921" dur="3.7">beautiful</text><text start="2751.521" dur="5.3">for</text><text start="2752.621" dur="6.7">heroes proved in</text><text start="2756.821" dur="2.5">liberating</text><text start="2759.521" dur="2.2">strife,</text><text start="2762.321" dur="2.1">who</text><text start="2764.521" dur="7.3">more than self their country loved,</text><text start="2769.521" dur="2.3">and mercy</text><text start="2773.221" dur="3">more than</text><text start="2774.121" dur="2.1">life.</text><text start="2776.721" dur="2.2">America,</text><text start="2780.921" dur="2.3">America,</text><text start="2783.821" dur="4.3">God shed</text><text start="2785.921" dur="4.466">his grace</text><text start="2788.121" dur="2.266">on thee, [singing]</text><text start="2791.421" dur="2.186">and</text><text start="2792.321" dur="2">crown</text><text start="2793.607" dur="2.314">[screaming]</text><text start="2794.321" dur="2.6">thy good</text><text start="2795.921" dur="3.2">with</text><text start="2796.921" dur="2.2">brotherhood</text><text start="2802.121" dur="4.6">from sea to</text><text start="2804.821" dur="4">shining</text><text start="2806.721" dur="2.1">sea.</text><text start="2809.321" dur="2.2">America,</text><text start="2812.121" dur="2.501">America.</text><text start="2812.602" dur="2.02">&amp;gt;&amp;gt; [screaming]</text><text start="2846.007" dur="2.02">[music]</text><text start="2848.922" dur="3.69">&amp;gt;&amp;gt; God bless America, [singing]</text><text start="2852.723" dur="8.8">land that I love. Stand beside her and</text><text start="2858.223" dur="7.399">guide her through the night with a light</text><text start="2861.523" dur="7.8">from above. From the mountains to the</text><text start="2865.622" dur="5.8">prairies, [singing] to the oceans white</text><text start="2869.323" dur="5.299">with foam,</text><text start="2871.422" dur="7.5">God bless America,</text><text start="2874.622" dur="7.601">my home sweet home.</text><text start="2878.922" dur="8.351">God bless America,</text><text start="2882.223" dur="5.705">my home sweet home.</text><text start="2887.273" dur="2.675">[music]</text><text start="2887.928" dur="2.02">[singing]</text><text start="2909.023" dur="7.5">God bless America,</text><text start="2912.223" dur="8.199">my home sweet home.</text><text start="2916.523" dur="8.599">God bless America,</text><text start="2920.422" dur="6.801">my home sweet</text><text start="2925.122" dur="2.101">home.</text><text start="2971.224" dur="2.3">&amp;gt;&amp;gt; Take your time.</text></transcript>